 "text": "Hi! How's life treating you? Simple things work best. Do you have any old family photos they' never seen? Put the album on the coffee table and let him talk while he looks. Grandparents love anything that keeps them going. Make sure anything with chicken or spaghetti is clearly marked. Then keep the salt away from the kitchen counter and out of her reach. Move it to a shelf high up, or give her own small jar. Same idea. Keep it in the fridge and keep it out of reach. A fruit platter with fruit she can reach is much safer.",
